{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261030T124922Z-54308d48", "ts": "2026-10-30T12:51:18Z", "actor": {"worktree": "arrt", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev.2", "branch": "fix/walls-stale-edit", "build": "0d265237c4dd"}, "body": {"base_commit": "3ba2812fcddab19daeee26b7f72c5da173102876", "base_tree": "12bef23b75786da1555bb0242882a5aa95dcaf51", "head_tree": "9b7ac46999275cc7fec0596b601be06e57712cb8", "head_commit": "3cd67b738dd213f213b052862762a5c4968fa7f0", "dispatch_commit": "3cd67b738dd213f213b052862762a5c4968fa7f0", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "rule-4 cumulative: working tree is clean, so chunk/final would dispatch an empty interval; branch is 1 commit(s) ahead of origin/develop and no cumulative record covers current HEAD \u2014 the committed bundle is cumulative's scope", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js", "arrt/tests/browser/test_displays_and_labels.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_hanging_a_theme.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_scenes_on_walls.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_the_walls.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/change-log.md", "arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js", "arrt/tests/browser/test_displays_and_labels.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_hanging_a_theme.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_scenes_on_walls.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_the_walls.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/change-log.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Edit\u2026 and Scene\u2026 now await a read before opening, with no guard on the press-to-open window: a second press opens a second dialog, and a navigation in between opens the dialog over the next page", "recommendation": "Class: every opener in walls.js that now awaits a read before openPanel (editWall, reached from both Edit\u2026 and 'Choose its Player\u2026'; sceneOpener's onclick). Before this change both handlers were synchronous, so neither problem could happen. Now: (a) a double-click on Edit\u2026 during the read (up to three requests: /api/walls, /api/clients, then /api/manifest) stacks two modal Edit dialogs, each with its own editing() state. On Scene\u2026, the second openPanel overwrites scene.panel, and closing the top dialog runs the first one's onClose (scene.panel = null) or orphans the first, so repaintScene paints into a dialog that is gone. (b) openPanel registers its hashchange close only once it has opened, so a curator who presses Edit\u2026 and then follows a nav link before the read returns gets a modal Walls dialog over the next page, which is the case openPanel's own comment says must not happen. Fix it once at the opener, not per handler: keep an in-flight flag (or disable the control) for the read, and before openPanel check that state.view is still 'walls' and the control is still connected. Add a browser test that presses Edit\u2026 twice in quick succession and asserts that exactly one dialog.panel-dialog exists.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "Edit\u2026's new failure path has no test, and its named branch ('it is no longer recorded') cannot be reached because nothing deletes a wall", "recommendation": "Instance. Before this change Edit\u2026 could not fail. Now a failed /api/walls read puts 'Couldn't open <wall>'s settings: \u2026' beside the control and opens nothing, and no test exercises that path. Add a browser test that makes /api/walls fail when Edit\u2026 is pressed (a page.route abort or 500 after the first paint) and asserts the sentence beside the control and that no dialog.panel-dialog exists. Also assert the absence on that path, per the learning 'When a clause or notice is conditional, assert its absence'. The change-log's 'A wall no longer recorded says so beside Edit\u2026 and opens nothing' describes a branch that nothing reaches. I grepped arrt/src for a wall delete (route, store method, or DELETE FROM walls) and found none; the only DELETE routes under /walls/{id} are /labels, /client and /theme. So either drop the branch and that change-log line, or keep the branch as defensive and make the change-log say so rather than describe it as user-visible behaviour. The reachable failure (a read that fails) is the one the test needs to cover.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js", "arrt/tests/browser/test_displays_and_labels.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Scene\u2026 re-reads the scene but still builds its wall rows from the page's last paint (scene.walls), the same stale shape this change fixes", "recommendation": "Instance of the fix's own class, per the learning 'When you fix a defect, make inputs the fix does not know fail by name, and grep the commit for the same shape'. sceneBuilder lists pickRow(scene, draft, wall) only over scene.walls, which was set at page paint, and inWallOrder orders by it too. A wall added since the paint (POST /api/walls from another tab or surface) has no row, so a draft pin on it is invisible in the dialog. The lead still says 'Preparing the walls\u2026' because pins.length counts it, and Apply shows it anyway. A wall renamed since the paint is offered under its old name. Read /api/walls alongside /api/scenes/live in sceneOpener and set scene.walls from that read. Add a case to the new test_a_draft_assembled_elsewhere\u2026 that pins a wall created after the paint and asserts the wall has a row.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js", "arrt/tests/browser/test_scenes_on_walls.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Async Edit\u2026 and Scene\u2026 openers have no in-flight guard: a second press during the read stacks a second modal, and Scene\u2026's single scene.panel slot then points at the wrong dialog", "recommendation": "Instance. Both openers now await a network read (Edit\u2026: /api/walls + /api/clients + the wall's manifest; Scene\u2026: /api/scenes/live) before openPanel's showModal makes the page inert, and nothing disables the control or ignores a press while that read is in flight (attempt() does not). A double-press opens two stacked dialogs. For Scene\u2026 the state then diverges: the second open overwrites scene.panel, and closing the first runs its onClose `scene.panel = null` while the second is still open, so every later paintScene/repaintScene returns before filling the visible dialog, and picks or Discard in it leave the dialog stale. For Edit\u2026, two independent editing() handles open over each other. The control also gives no sign that the press registered while the manifest is being built. Fix: set the control busy (disabled, or a module-level 'opening' flag per opener) for the duration of the read and clear it in a finally, and in sceneOpener make onClose clear scene.panel only when it still holds the panel being closed. A browser test that clicks twice before the dialog opens would pin it.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Edit\u2026's fresh read turns 'the manifest could not be read' into the same silent absence as 'nothing is hung': Rotation, Shapes and Mat disappear with no sentence", "recommendation": "Instance. editWall does `manifest = (await built(wall)).manifest || null`, and built() returns {failure} on an error, so a failed manifest read opens the dialog without playbackPanels and matPanel and says nothing. Before this change the manifest came from the paint, where the same failure also put the card in its 'unreachable' reason, so the curator had been told; now the dialog's own read can fail when the page's did not, and the curator sees settings that are simply missing. Learnings core: 'When a check can be quiet for more than one reason, give each quiet state its own output...'. Distinguish the two: when built() returns a failure, either fail the whole read through attempt() (it already says 'Couldn't open X's settings \u2014 \u2026' beside the control) or put a one-line note where those panels would be. The no-theme case stays as accepted earlier (prior R-2/R-8).", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "The rule 'read when pressed, never from the page's last paint' is stated in two comments and applied to two openers; other dialogs built from the paint remain", "recommendation": "Class. The fix writes a general principle into editWall's comment but has no shared owner. Other openers still build from the paint: theme.js Hang\u2026 (placement.hanging_on), clients.js Edit <Player> (token_issued_at and the rest), and walls.js' card acts built from paint-time `themes`/`manifest`. Learnings core: 'When you fix a defect, make inputs the fix does not know fail by name, and grep the commit for the same shape'. The ones checked are mostly harmless, because Hang\u2026 works out its hang/take-down from the diff against the set it painted, so this stays a note. If the principle is meant to bind, the construction is one helper (for example openFresh(control, read, build)) that every dialog opener uses. That would also be the one place to put the in-flight guard from the finding above. Otherwise, narrow the comment to the cases it covers. Search: every `openPanel(` call site under http/static whose body reads a variable captured at paint time.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Render comment still says the scene line and the Scene\u2026 dialog are 'painted from the same read'", "recommendation": "Instance; prose, and nothing reads it. In render(), the comment above `const scene = \u2026` says the line above the cards and the Scene\u2026 dialog are both painted from the same read, by paintScene. After this change the dialog paints from its own read, taken when Scene\u2026 is pressed, and that read repaints the line too. Make the claim relational ('both are painted by paintScene, from whichever read is newest') or delete its second sentence. No other edit is wanted.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Edit\u2026 drops the rotation, shapes and mat panels without saying why when the wall's feed cannot be read at press time", "recommendation": "editWall now reads the manifest when the button is pressed, and does it with `(await built(wall)).manifest || null`. That throws away `built`'s `{failure}`. If that read fails (even briefly) while /api/walls succeeds, the dialog opens with no playback panels and no mat panel, and nothing explains the gap. A curator reasonably concludes the wall has no such settings. Before this change the same omission was explained, because the card showed the paint's own manifest failure. Now the card can show a good feed while the dialog quietly loses the panels. Scope: instance. Either state `built`'s failure in the dialog where those panels would go, or throw inside the `attempt` so the failure is reported beside Edit\u2026, the way a wall that is no longer recorded is.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: brookstalley/arrt#400 'curation-ui: a wall's Edit\u2026 opened before a repaint shows stale state'", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Verify it, then call `/prawduct:backlog update 400 status=shipped closed-by=scope:walls-stale-edit` when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says. The change-log's 'Closes #400' does nothing if this merges into develop rather than the default branch, the same as #181 and #324 earlier. `affecting` over the five subject files returned only #400. No other open curation-ui item covers Walls' dialogs. C-B1, C-B2 and C-B4: nothing applies (#400 resolves; no new items).", "files": [".prawduct/change-log.md"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings cross-check: core.md and surface.md read; nothing escalates", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The read list came from `learnings-files --for-diff`: core.md and surface.md. No rule changed this cycle. 'When you fix a defect, make inputs the fix does not know fail by name, and grep the commit for the same shape': the input the fix does not know, a wall that is gone, fails by name ('it is no longer recorded; reload the page'). Grepping walls.js's other openPanel sites for the same paint-snapshot shape found two. 'Remove \u2026 from <wall>' acts on the painted `card.now.workId`, but that is the work the card visibly shows, so it is what the curator chose. The 'N works can't be shown here\u2026' panel is read-only and uses the painted manifest. Neither offers a write option that a write elsewhere has made stale, which was #400's shape. 'Before a UI or notice says do X to fix this': the advice to reload has a working remedy. No rule-unenforced finding: none of these rules is written so that a check could own it here.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/walls.js"], "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: covered .prawduct/change-log.md (the walls-stale-edit entry); nothing clears a bar", "recommendation": "Scope: none. I checked the entry's claims against the diff. Edit\u2026 reads /api/walls, the client listing and the wall's manifest when pressed: true. A wall that is no longer recorded is said beside the control and opens nothing (`attempt`): true. Scene\u2026 reads /api/scenes/live when pressed: true. One count is inert: 'Four existing tests \u2026 now wait for it to open'. The diff adds waits to two (test_hanging_a_theme, test_the_walls), and test_displays_and_labels gets only a comment rewrite. Nothing reads that figure, and no edit is wanted.", "files": [".prawduct/change-log.md"], "fid": "R-11"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 5, "note": 6}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/walls-stale-edit`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "3ba2812fcddab19daeee26b7f72c5da173102876", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/change-log.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-10-30T12:49:23Z"}}

