painted page, from a control that is no longer connected. Prior R-1 asked for both checks. Key the guard on the wall (or on editWall itself) rather than the control, and add `control.isConnected` to the late-arrival check. Accept or ride the next commit; it is narrow (the second opener only appears when the wall has an assignment problem).", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261030T124922Z-54308d48", "fid": "R-1"}, "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Edit\u2026's reachable failure path (a failed /api/walls or Players read) is still untested", "recommendation": "Instance. The change-log half of R-2 is settled ('nothing removes a wall yet, so it waits on #391'). The test half is not: no browser test makes /api/walls (or the client listing) fail when Edit\u2026 is pressed and asserts the 'Couldn't open <wall>'s settings: \u2026' sentence beside the control and that no dialog.panel-dialog exists. The only /api/walls 500 test (test_the_walls.py:362) is the page-level read. The new feed-failure test covers built()'s failure, a different branch.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261030T124922Z-54308d48", "fid": "R-2"}, "oid": "O-2"}], "duration_seconds": 240, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/walls-stale-edit`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/change-log.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-10-30T12:59:06Z"}}

